  "details": "\"In a crowded room with numerous people, it becomes challenging to hear conversations clearly when everyone is speaking simultaneously, especially with a good friend or multiple friends. To address this, I propose the addition of a gaze feature. This feature would allow users to click on a specific person, designating them as the focus. When the focused person speaks, the volume of others' voices would be attenuated, prioritized based on the sound levels. The sensitivity of this comparison could be adjusted in the menu, similar to grouping individuals based on sound priority. It's crucial that this feature supports simultaneous focus on a minimum of five individuals, preferably around ten. In large, mixed environments, this functionality should not require the consent of the focused individuals. The current feature of adjusting the volume for specific individuals is not effective in rooms with a high number of participants, as each person has varying microphone volumes.\"",
